/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  species/HGlyc.dat -- ONE model species, ONE typed file: the most protonated form of glycolic acid, the speciation MASTER of its family.
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv, which holds every
  reading (source, table, page, whether read from a page image).  Standard state: ideal solution at
  1 mol/kg, 298.15 K, H+ = 0.
  NO `aqueousThermo` ON PURPOSE: the ionisation (pK, dH) of glycolic acid is printed in Miller & Smith-Magowan Table 6, so the SPECIATION is complete.  Its formation data are NOT entered: Miller Table 5 (p. 1056) prints dHf(cr) -664.0, dH(soln) +15.94 and dHf(aq acid) -651.0, which do not close (-664.0 + 15.94 = -648.06, 2.9 kJ/mol from the printed aqueous value, the row marked error estimated); the NBS tables print glycolate -652.3 (dHf only, no entropy).  Three readings disagree by 4.7 kJ/mol and the work in hand does not say which is right, so the energy route through glycolate REFUSES BY NAME.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType modelSpecies;
schemaVersion 1;

name    HGlyc;
formula     "HC2H3O3";
charge  0;
MW { value 76.051; unit g/mol;}
